      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "$$\n{{0\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{1\\}=\\{1,2\\}}}\\,\\overset{∨}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{or}}}\\,\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{2}{3}\\text{ is irrational}}}}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∨R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∨(Q∨R)$ is {{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q∨R$ is false, but the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{true}∨\\overset{\\text{false}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∨\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
